@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Download Automation - Demo Page";
}

<div id="content">
    <!--  CONTENT   -->
    <div id="page-header" class="page-demo">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="span12 whitebg">
                <h1>Demo <span>File Download</span> Automation</h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">


        <div class="span12">

            <p>In a few seconds SeeShell will <a href="http://www.7-zip.org/"> click this link</a>, which will bring you to the 7zip download page. Once there, Kantu will 
            trigger the file download. By default, you find all downloaded files in the <em>your user</em>/documents/SeeShell.Browser/downloads</em>
            folder.

            <p>
                This demo shows how to use SeeShell for automating file downloads.

            </p>
            <p>
                By the way: While we are not affiliated with 7-zip.org in any way, 
                7zip is a great compression tool. We use it daily.

            </p>
 



        </div>
    </div>
</div>
